// What a callee's spec claims it returns.
//
// spec_return rows come from two places (Argus.Extractors.Specs): the
// analyzed beams' own specs, and the specs of the remote functions they
// call as installed on the code path. A function the program defines is
// read only from the program — the installed copy of an analyzed module
// may be an older build — and everything else from the code path.
//
// A spec is a claim nothing verified. Rules read callee_returns to stay
// quiet about a callee whose spec rules out what they ask about, or to
// confirm what they already derived; never to report on a spec alone. A
// callee with no row is unknown (no spec, a term() return, a module
// shipped without specs), which is not the same as "cannot fail".
//
// Requires imports.dl.

.decl callee_returns(func: symbol, shape: symbol)

callee_returns(f, shape) :- spec_return(f, shape, "analyzed").

callee_returns(f, shape) :-
  spec_return(f, shape, "installed"),
  !function_def(f, _, _, _, _).
